From 12c7e7ecabb2e7c1bb9f1ec0dd2c2ebfdea0b7b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Icenowy Zheng <zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 16:14:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 003/344] FROMGIT: arm64: dts: qcom:
 sc8280xp-lenovo-thinkpad-x13s: set GPI DMA channels

It's found that some GPI interfaces shouldn't be touched by HLOS,
otherwise system hang / reset happens.

The GPI interface availability information is available via the ACPI
DSDT table, as interrupt resources for \_SB_.QGP* devices.

Add such information to the device tree file.

The DSDT table is acquired at [1].

[1] https://github.com/aarch64-laptops/build/blob/5e03e2900dee80877895342fa62f9a1badc785d8/misc/lenovo-thinkpad-x13s/dsdt.dsl

Signed-off-by: Icenowy Zheng <zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260602081451.3808833-4-zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Andersson <andersson@kernel.org>

(cherry picked from commit efc4bb04c5aaf3ef65033f8b8b9e1d50b76cd62f
 https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/qcom/linux.git for-next)
Signed-off-by: Kexy Biscuit <kexybiscuit@aosc.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-lenovo-thinkpad-x13s.dts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-lenovo-thinkpad-x13s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-lenovo-thinkpad-x13s.dts
index 218573a97785b..77d3c7af3643f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-lenovo-thinkpad-x13s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-lenovo-thinkpad-x13s.dts
@@ -705,14 +705,17 @@ &dispcc0 {
 };
 
 &gpi_dma0 {
+	dma-channel-mask = <0x3>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &gpi_dma1 {
+	dma-channel-mask = <0x3>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &gpi_dma2 {
+	dma-channel-mask = <0x3>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-- 
